Z||000000||pontiacs4me||02-26-2001||02:46 AM||||ok heres another problem im having, my emergency brake light is always on, unless I push in the button on the ebrake and push it down real hard.  If I let off of it it stays until I hit a little bump then it clicks back out and the light comes back on and the thing in the dash that goes "bong, bong, bong" starts going off, and it is real annoying.  What can I do to adjust this?  Ive already decided to find the bonging device and unplug it.  I hate those things.  I can even hear it when it isnt making any noise.  thanks in advance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||02-26-2001||05:53 AM||||Your cable isn't completely releasing, may have slack. Try pulling the cable to the rear where it crosses the cradle and see if that stops the warning. If so it needs adjusting at this same point. Could indicate worn rear pads which translate to slack in the cable.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||02-26-2001||07:23 AM||||The switch is mounted at the base of the E-brake lever underneath the boot.  To get to it you'll need to remove the plastic trim piece that covers the opening along the door.  Remove the round metal plugs (they simply pry out) to expose about 7 hex head bolts (I believe they are around 10mm).  Maneuver the trim up and over the e-brake handle and out of the car.  The boot should simply lift off now.  The switch is at the base of the lever.  You may be able to adjust it slightly.<P>Try adjusting the cable first though as mentioned above.  Your lever should click no more than about 8 times as you apply the brake.<P>Does your e-brake actually engage and hold?  If the cable is adjusted to tightly it won't let the lever return to it's stop and connect the switch.<P>Looking under the car at the e-brake levers on the rear calipers, when the brake is released the levers should be completely against the stop.  If not, the cable is too tight.<P>Hope this helps.  If not ask again and I'll try again.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000003||pontiacs4me||02-26-2001||11:09 AM||||I rebuilt all the rear braking system when I did my engine swap.  I tested the ebrake yesterday, I pulled it all the way up and I was only slowing down slightly.  Im going to try to tighten the adjusting nut a few turns and hopefully the light will go off.  Im replacing the carpet in a few weeks so Ill find the switch and do something with it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||pontiacs4me||02-26-2001||11:09 AM||||I rebuilt all the rear braking system when I did my engine swap.  I tested the ebrake yesterday, I pulled it all the way up and I was only slowing down slightly.  Im going to try to tighten the adjusting nut a few turns and hopefully the light will go off.  Im replacing the carpet in a few weeks so Ill find the switch and do something with it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||pontiacs4me||02-26-2001||03:10 PM||||sorry about the double post above, but anyway I fixed the brake light problem, I just tightened the adjusting nut about 5 turns and it turned off.  thanks.||||reg||1
